From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Rowley <johnrowleyster@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 21:54:06 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Add window classes, a message queue and dialog stubs to
 miniwin

miniwin gains the USER32 subset a Win32 game's WinMain needs to run over
SDL3: RegisterClassA, CreateWindowExA, DestroyWindow, DefWindowProcA,
PeekMessageA, TranslateMessage, DispatchMessageA, PostQuitMessage,
SendMessageA, ShowWindow, UpdateWindow, SetActiveWindow, SetFocus,
SetCapture, ReleaseCapture, SetWindowTextA, GetWindowRect, GetClientRect,
GetDesktopWindow, AdjustWindowRect, SetWindowLongA, MoveWindow,
ShowCursor, SetCursor, GetCursorPos, SetCursorPos, ScreenToClient and
MessageBoxA. SDL events become WM_* messages for the window's procedure.
Dialog boxes need resource templates, so DialogBoxParamA, EndDialog,
GetDlgItem and EnableWindow are declared and fail.

Also: POINT, MSG, WNDCLASSA, WINDOWPOS, the message and control
constants, one-rectangle regions (CreateRectRgn, GetRegionData,
OffsetRect), D3DRMVectorRandom and D3DRMVectorRotate, D3DDEVICEDESC's
dwDevCaps and D3DDD_* flags, DDLOCK_NOSYSLOCK and DirectDrawEnumerateA.

